  description="The bronzing of Addison's disease is one of medicine's most elegant physical signs — and it is pure melanocortin biology. A failing adrenal gland makes the pituitary flood the body with ACTH, and because ACTH carries α-MSH inside it, that flood darkens the skin through the same MC1R pigment switch a tanning drug uses."
